side_effects: "The damage to mental stability is as pronounced as the regular Crazy''s, with increasingly intense insanities as time goes on (the book gives no schedule of its own and points to the Crazy). Many TW Crazies eventually develop Power by Association, and with magic belief is reality: when the condition behind the delusion is absent, or when a phobia strikes and the save vs insanity (12 or higher) fails, the character loses his combat bonuses, heightened senses and supernatural P.S., and his M.D.C. is halved."
extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 131-133 (cache p131-p133, page_offset 0); the lore opens on 131, the powers and first O.C.C. Skills are on 132, the rest of the block on 133. Printed 132 checked against a 110 dpi render; the OCR agreed on every number, and its ''0.C.C. Skills'' is O.C.C. Skills. No ultra-crazy class was in production on 2026-09-25; the crazy class names this one as not extracted. || XP: the Ojahee ''Borg, Ultra-Crazy and Arkhon Spectral Hunter ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed. Level 14 prints 400,000, below the 400,001 the pattern implies - a book slip, stored as printed since it still rises strictly. || GROUP: filed under the Silver River Republics'' O.C.C.s with no group heading; stored as men-of-arms, the crazy precedent. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || POOLS: M.D.C. 3D6x10 + P.E., +2D4 per level, as mdc_base. P.P.E. 1D6x10. I.S.P. M.E. x5 plus 2D6 per level as isp_base. No hit points or S.D.C. are printed (an M.D.C. creature). Not supersedes_race: the conversion is built for human psychics and the book never says the character stops being what it was, so a race stating its own M.D.C., P.P.E. or money wins a pairing - the class-check warning, accepted. || ATTRIBUTES: +2D4 P.S. (minimum 17), +5D6 Spd, +1D6 P.P. (minimum 17) as dice attribute bonuses and attribute_minimums, the crazy precedent. Supernatural P.S. (mega-damage punches) is prose in the ability. || BONUSES: +4 roll, +2 initiative, +1 attack; +2 save vs magic (spell_magic) and psionics, +6 vs mind control, +4 vs toxic gases, poisons and drugs (toxins_poisons and harmful_drugs, as the crazy stores the same line), +10% vs coma/death. The +5% to delicate-touch skills and the power-loss penalties are conditional and are prose. || PSIONICS: master. Six powers from any category except Super (a starting group of Sensitive, Physical and Healing); one more from any category, Super included, at levels 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 and 13. categories_allowed includes Super so the schedule reaches it. No exclusions printed. || INSANITY: the book says only ''like the regular Crazy'' and prints no table or schedule; the crazy class''s RUE schedule is not copied here, because this book''s reference is to the 1990 Rifts RPG and the two may differ. The power-loss rule is an ability and the side effects. || SKILLS: Spanish 98 as Language: Spanish; Literacy: Spanish (+15%) as Literacy: Native Language 40+15; Radio: Basic 45+10; Acrobatics 30+10; Climbing 40+15; Prowl 25+20; Land Navigation 36+10; Horsemanship (+15%) as Horsemanship: General 40+15. W.P. Ancient two and W.P. Modern two as Weapon Proficiencies picks (the catalog files no ancient/modern split), W.P. Energy Rifle. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil with no price printed: costs { assassin: 0 }, the crazy precedent; no other style is offered. || RELATED: six, plus one W.P. and two skills at level 3, two at 6, one at 9 and 12 (3/2/1/1; the W.P. part is the note). Bonuses as printed: Communications +5, Espionage +10, Military +5, Physical +10, Rogue +5, Technical +5; Domestic, Pilot, Pilot Related, Science, W.P. and Wilderness any; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Mechanical Automotive (Automotive Mechanics) and Locksmith only; Medical Paramedic and Holistic (Holistic Medicine) only. No Horsemanship or Cowboy line, so neither category is granted. || SECONDARY: four from the same list, no bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: M.D.C. body armor as a choice led by this book''s armor; riding clothing as traveling-clothes; the black or camouflage jump-suit as black-clothing-covert; two ancient weapons from the crazy''s catalog set; a vibro-blade of choice; two energy weapons from a catalog set; eight E-clips (four each); survival kit; camp knife as knife; a light personal vehicle from the catalog set (the horse-borg and horse-bot have no row and are not stubbed). || MONEY: 1D4x1000 credits. || CYBERNETICS: none other than the M.O.M. implants, as a restriction."
