## Lore

Argentina was where M.O.M. Works first developed the Crazy conversion, and its
old research centres came through the Great Cataclysm with little damage.
Researchers from Santiago rebuilt one, led by Professor Nostradamus Cervantes,
a Techno-Wizard and authority on the conversion who was convinced that an
ordinary Crazy could never stand up to a gargoyle, a brodkil or a Pucara giant
hand to hand. His team blended magic, technology and psionics to push the
process further, at the cost of many volunteers killed, driven catatonic,
possessed or sent berserk in experiments the Santiago government never learned
the truth about. The first Techno-Wizard M.O.M. system appeared in 93 P.A.; by
100 P.A. more than three thousand TW Crazies served Santiago and its smaller
neighbours, many of them in the army''s Special Legion.

The candidates are minor or major psychics. The magically powered implants
mutate the brain, making the subject a master psionic, and the psychic energy
pouring from it turns the body supernatural: mega-damage tough, strong enough
to fight a young dragon barehanded. The price is the Crazy''s madness and worse.
Many Ultra-Crazies come to believe their power flows from some source, and
because magic makes belief real, they truly lose it when that source is gone.
They patrol the plains between Santiago''s cities in small scouting units,
often mounted on horse-borgs or horse-bots, hunting raiders and monsters.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ultra-crazy');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ultra-crazy';

